    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "letting it go sounds nice in theory, but it's hard when the \"letting go\" feels like it can only mean one thing. it's like i'm finished with my part in the story. once the mission is complete and there's nothing left to do or be, why does it feel so wrong to just... stop? it feels like the only sense left is in the exit.",
